WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.899
Good morning, Hank, it's Wednesday and this
is the beginning of my zombie apocalypse novella:

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:08.200
"Pre-zombification, my father was already
obsessed with corn. He told me almost every

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.300
day that corn was in control of us. Corn wants
the world to contain more corn, so corn evolves

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.010
us to agree with it: Corn tells us that we
could make sugar out of corn, or fuel out

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:24.970
of corn, or plastic out of corn, etc. The
flu makes us cough, which spreads the flu.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:30.350
Corn makes us corn-hungry, which spreads corn.
He got this idea from a book, and he never

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.970
ceased to be amazed by it. For years, he would
talk about it. We’d be eating mashed potatoes

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.180
or something, and he’d say, “You know,
potatoes are impossible without corn. That

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.780
corn, it’s everywhere.” (He meant this
metaphorically, although it is now nearly

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.780
true literally.)

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.399
I think my dad was so fascinated by this idea
because he realized on some fundamental level

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:54.190
that he was not in control of his desires:
I think he woke up every morning in his nice

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:59.559
house with hardwood floors and granite countertops
and wondered why he desired granite countertops

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:05.269
and hardwood floors, wondered who precisely
was running his life. Most people never stop

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:09.659
to wonder why they like Pop Tarts or rainflow
showerheads or skinny girls or whatever it

00:01:09.659 --> 00:01:14.200
is they like. Although my father never abandoned
the narrowly circumscribed suburban life he

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.819
was fated to desire, the why of it all nagged
at him. I inherited that penchant for intellectualism,

00:01:19.819 --> 00:01:25.229
a character flaw that these days can only
be thoroughly eradicated by getting Z’ed

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:26.229
up.

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:29.300
Anyway, I have been thinking about the old
man because it was a year ago today that I

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.399
shot him in the chest with a hollow-point
.45 caliber bullet. He kind of smiled as he

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:38.030
fell backwards onto the overstuffed living
room couch. He took a minute to die, and it

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.369
was the smilingest minute I’d ever seen
from him.

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:43.829
A lot of the Z’ed up smile when you kill
them. I don’t know if they’re grateful

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:49.240
or amused or what, but it helps with the guilt,
which quite a lot of people feel. I knew a

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.969
kid once who was the kind of sentimentalist
who found it troubling to think of himself

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:57.910
as a murderer, so he called killing Zs completing
them. I liked that.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:01.959
That kid—his name was Marcos Marcos—got
Z’ed up somehow. We were living in a very

00:02:01.959 --> 00:02:06.619
nice heavily chandeliered Lincoln Park townhouse
with a few other humanoid types, and then

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:11.110
one morning Marcos Marcos made a go at my
puppy, Mr. President, and I had to complete

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:15.379
him. I completed his head all over the dining
room credenza of that fancy townhouse and

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:19.040
then me and Mr. President bolted out for the
proverbial higher ground.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.349
Newzies go for dogs and cats and cows first,
because they’ve still got enough of a moral

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:28.040
compass to recognize that separating human
beings from their vital organs—aside from

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.200
being ethically troubling—is cannibalistic.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.850
It is my own moral compass that has done me
in now, working through the last few gallons

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:39.500
of the gas that runs the generator that pumps
the putrid Z’ed out air down here into my

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:43.120
Lincoln Square cellar, eating through the
last rusted cans of diced tomatoes and Spam,

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.709
drinking very expensive red wine at the rate
of precisely one bottle per day, watching

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:54.860
the shelves empty out, wondering—as my father
did—what terrible monster lurking inside

00:02:54.860 --> 00:03:00.549
of me forces me to go on rowing against the
current when I could just walk up a staircase,

00:03:00.549 --> 00:03:05.060
unlock this cellar door, and get Z’ed up
like a normal person."

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:08.220
So, Hank, that's the first page of my zombie
apocalypse novella which will never be published,

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:13.189
not because I dislike zombie apocalypse novellas
but because mine is BAD. That's by far the

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:15.469
best page of it, it gets much worse from there.

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:19.840
However, the only copy of my zombie apocalypse
novella that will ever exist will be just

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:25.260
one of many amazing Project For Awesome raffle
prizes. Speaking of which, Nerdfighters, I

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.680
hope you're hard at work on your Project For
Awesome videos. If you want to know more about

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.260
what the Project For Awesome is, look in my
points. (points rapidly)

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.709
Hank, I don't want to give too much away but
on December seventeenth and eighteenth Project

00:03:33.709 --> 00:03:38.769
For Awesome videos are going to be featured
ALL OVER YOUTUBE so Nerdfighters make those

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:44.209
Project For Awesome videos awesome. DFTBA
like it says on my shirt, Hank, I'll see you

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:44.779
on Friday.

